From: nuubOS <nuubos@localhost>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 20:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Picture in picture at 2x with a shrunk corner screen
 (nuubOS)

Picture in Picture built a 768x576 frame (main screen 3x, the corner one
at its own size): Mario Kart DS kept the four cores full copying it
(55-58 fps, the other layouts 60). The main screen is now doubled and
the corner screen shrunk to 2/3 (171x128, every 3x3 block to 2x2 with
2:1 weights) before the 3:1 blend: the same place and a third of the
width as before in a 512x384 frame (0.79 MB a frame instead of 1.77).
The panels already showed the corner screen below its own size (160
lines on 640x480). The stylus cursor is drawn on a full-size copy of
the touch screen before it is shrunk, and pointer touches map through
the shrunk size (touch_w/touch_h). Mario Kart DS race: 57-61 fps,
mostly 60.
